    "working_name_not_printed": "고르는 동작을 새기는 시트론 잉크 삽화",
    "whole_relationship": "Two differently branching plants and two deliberate hands create a comparison by habit, scale and handling. The bright field is occupied by chunky printed plant/hand forms and their weight-bearing pots, not a passive information board. The left Title/body sequence can remain familiar while the image, letter voice and colour rhythm are markedly different.",
    "positive_direction": "A vivid citron and aubergine ink world with restrained burnt-orange touch points. Hand-drawn lithographic contours, chunky flat plant masses, sparse directional hatching and precise overprinted silhouettes make a confident graphic illustration. Use real-looking plant habit and adult hands, with irregular but controlled drawn edges. The Title has generous bold Korean sans shape and decisiveness; regular body is sharply printed, separated from the image’s grain. A hand gently tests the scale of a compact upright plant while another supports the broad-leaf plant at the edge of its pot. Distinguish the two growing habits and keep hand/pot/stem contact readable. Make the choice feel active through reach and touch, without adding fake comparison labels, arrows, numbers or a cute shopping mascot. The image is an authored ink illustration, not a 3D clay pot or leaf wreath.",
    "native_positive_brief": "Create one finished opaque flat landscape 16:9 poster. Use the supplied newly authored planning guide for actual copy anatomy, readable areas and substantive image contacts; implement the following completed style rather than reproducing its temporary shapes. A vivid citron and aubergine ink world with restrained burnt-orange touch points. Hand-drawn lithographic contours, chunky flat plant masses, sparse directional hatching and precise overprinted silhouettes make a confident graphic illustration. Use real-looking plant habit and adult hands, with irregular but controlled drawn edges. The Title has generous bold Korean sans shape and decisiveness; regular body is sharply printed, separated from the image’s grain. A hand gently tests the scale of a compact upright plant while another supports the broad-leaf plant at the edge of its pot. Distinguish the two growing habits and keep hand/pot/stem contact readable. Make the choice feel active through reach and touch, without adding fake comparison labels, arrows, numbers or a cute shopping mascot. The image is an authored ink illustration, not a 3D clay pot or leaf wreath. Two differently branching plants and two deliberate hands create a comparison by habit, scale and handling. The bright field is occupied by chunky printed plant/hand forms and their weight-bearing pots, not a passive information board. The left Title/body sequence can remain familiar while the image, letter voice and colour rhythm are markedly different. The intended feeling is Open, energetic and social; exploring the market has the confidence of a lively printed cultural poster. Make the supplied main Title immediately recognisable through its broad size, weight/contrast and breathing space. Keep the market line as a subordinate eyebrow, the English name as a smaller companion, and the short explanatory sentence as a clear Subtitle. Keep the entire explanatory paragraph as mature regular body text with stable starts, natural Korean word spaces and meaning-led soft lines. Link its ending to the date/hour/place group, then nearby access/care information, invitation and URL along the same optical axis. Keep footer bodies clearly readable, with clean digits and original en-dashes drawn as distinct long midline bars. Choose harmonious Korean, Latin and numeral anatomy; image texture does not damage small text. All typography is part of the native finished image; do not add a later SVG/font overlay. Respect the supplied roles and all original punctuation without adding labels, numbers, logos, QR, watermarks or other print. This is a complete poster, with content-bearing imagery and precise letter finish. Print only the following twelve entries, each exactly once:\n\n집 안의 작은 숲\nLEAVES & LIVING\n초록을 고르고, 일상을 가꿉니다.\n작은 화분부터 오래 키운 나무까지 만납니다. 재배자의 이야기를 듣고, 우리 집의 빛과 생활에 맞는 식물을 골라보세요.\n성수 주말 식물 마켓\n2027.06.12–06.13\n토·일 11:00–19:00\n성수 온실마당\n입장 무료 · 분갈이 시연\n식물 구매 시 관리 안내 제공\n편하게 들러 천천히 둘러보세요.\nleaves.example/market",
